::: outcomes
- Sign in through the single entrance and reach the admin panel.
- Edit every part of the public website.
- Create courses and lectures, and decide which student sees what.
- Turn any lecture material into a sheet with Claude and publish it.
- Know exactly what a student can see, print and download.
:::

::: timeplan
0-3   | Notation; @def:site
3-6   | Signing in; @thm:door
6-9   | Website content; @alg:content
9-14  | Courses, students, access; @thm:access
14-18 | Lectures and sheets; @alg:sheet
18-20 | Students' view; troubleshooting
:::

## Notation

::: definition "The website" {#def:site}
The website is the triple $\mathcal W=(\mathcal P,\ \mathcal S,\ \mathcal A)$ where
(1) $\mathcal P$ = the [[public pages]]: Home, About, Research, Publications, Courses, Contact — open to everyone;
(2) $\mathcal S$ = the [[student area]]: lectures, sheets, videos and files — open only to approved students;
(3) $\mathcal A$ = the [[admin panel]] — open only to you.
:::

Throughout, $S$ is the set of registered students, $C$ the set of courses, and $L(c)$ the set of lectures of a course $c\in C$.

::: columns
```graph layout=circle
Visitor -> Public : browse
Student -> Public : browse
Student -> Lectures : if approved
Doctor -> Admin : manage
Admin -> Lectures : publish
Admin -> Public : edit
```
+++
::: remark
Every page exists in **Arabic and English** (button عربي / EN at the top) and in a **day and night mode** (moon button). The choice is remembered on each device.
:::
:::

## Signing In

::: theorem "One door" {#thm:door}
There is exactly one sign-in page, **ahmadelajou.com/login**, for students and for you. After signing in, the website applies the map
$$\rho:\ \text{account}\longmapsto\begin{cases}\text{/admin/dashboard}, & \text{if the account is the admin},\\ \text{/dashboard}, & \text{if the account is a student.}\end{cases}$$
:::

::: howto "Signing in"
1. Open **ahmadelajou.com** and press the gold **Sign in** button at the top.
2. Enter your e-mail and password, then press **Sign in**.
3. You arrive at the admin panel. The gold **Admin panel** button at the top of every page brings you back to it.
4. To leave, press the **Sign out** button (⟶) at the top right.
:::

::: caution
Never share the admin password. Anyone with it can change the whole website.
:::

## The Admin Panel

The top bar of the admin panel has the same look as the website:

| Item | What it opens |
|:---|:---|
| **Overview** | numbers, waiting student requests, quick actions |
| **Courses & students** | courses, lectures, requests, students |
| **Website content ▾** | Profile, Publications, Research areas, News, Education, Positions, Awards, Memberships, Committees, Conferences, Supervision |
| **Sheet guide** | ready example sheets in both versions |
| **Student view** | the student area exactly as a student sees it |
| **View site** | the public website as a visitor sees it |

On a phone, the button ☰ opens the same menu.

## Website Content

::: definition "A content item" {#def:item}
A [[content item]] is one row of a section (one publication, one award, one position, …). Each section is a finite list $\{x_1,\dots,x_n\}$ of items.
:::

::: howto "Changing the public website" {#alg:content}
1. **Website content ▾** → choose the section.
2. **Add** to create an item, ✏️ to edit one, 🗑 to delete one.
3. Fill the fields (Arabic and English when both exist) and press **Save**.
:::

::: proposition "Immediate update"
A saved change appears on the public website **immediately**; in the worst case within one hour.
:::

::: remarks
(1) **Publications:** the switch **Featured** shows the paper on the home page. Citation counts are updated by hand from Google Scholar.
(2) **Profile:** name, title, biography in both languages, academic links, and the CV (PDF).
(3) **Supervision:** the student's name has an Arabic and an English field; each appears in its own language.
:::

## Courses, Students and Access

::: definition "Course" {#def:course}
A course $c\in C$ has a name (Arabic and English), a code (e.g. MATH 371), and two switches:
- **Published:** $c$ appears on the Courses page;
- **Accept new access requests:** students may ask to join $c$.
:::

Create one from **Courses & students → New course**. Inside a course there are five tabs: **Lectures**, **Course files**, **Announcements**, **Students**, **Settings**.

::: definition "Enrollment" {#def:enroll}
A student registers alone (name, university ID, university e-mail ending in `@std.bau.edu.jo`, phone), opens a course and presses **Request access**. This creates a pair $(s,c)$ in the [[enrollment relation]] $E\subseteq S\times C$ with a status
$$\sigma(s,c)\in\{\text{pending},\ \text{approved},\ \text{rejected}\}.$$
:::

```diagram
flow: Request access -> pending -> {Doctor decides} -yes-> approved
```

| Button (in **Courses & students → Requests**) | Effect on $\sigma(s,c)$ |
|:---|:---|
| **Approve** | pending $\to$ approved |
| **Reject** | pending $\to$ rejected |
| **Revoke** | approved $\to$ rejected (later, if needed) |
| **Block account** | the student loses **every** course at once |

::: theorem "Access" {#thm:access}
A student $s$ can open lecture $\ell\in L(c)$ !!if and only if!! all four conditions hold:
$$\sigma(s,c)=\text{approved},\qquad s\ \text{is not blocked},\qquad \ell\ \text{is published},\qquad \text{its sheet is shown}.$$ {#eq:access}
:::

::: corollary "Courses are independent"
Approving $s$ in $c_1$ gives **no** access to $c_2\neq c_1$: every course is decided separately.
:::

::: keybox
A student sees nothing of a course until **you** approve him in **that** course.
:::

## Lectures and Sheets

Inside a course: **Lectures → Add lecture**. Each lecture $\ell$ has the following parts:

| Part | Meaning |
|:---|:---|
| **Published to students** | $\ell$ appears to approved students |
| **Show student sheet** | the sheet appears with the solutions hidden |
| **Release solved (doctor) sheet** | the solved sheet appears — keep it off until you decide |
| **Student sheet** | the lecture file (`.mn`) |
| **Videos** | YouTube links (upload the video as **Unlisted**) |
| **Files** | PDFs or links; every PDF is stamped with the student's ID when downloaded |

::: definition "One file, two sheets" {#def:twosheets}
From one lecture file $F$ the website builds two sheets
$$\Phi(F)=\big(D(F),\ T(F)\big),$$
the [[doctor sheet]] $D(F)$ (everything visible) and the [[student sheet]] $T(F)=D(F)$ with every solution, answer and hidden proof replaced by blank writing lines, and the multiple-choice questions made interactive.
:::

::: remark
A separate solved file is possible (**Advanced**), but needed only when the two versions really differ.
:::

### Writing a sheet with Claude

::: howto "From lecture material to a published sheet" {#alg:sheet}
1. Open the Claude project **«Lecture Sheets»**.
2. Send anything: a PDF, a Word file, slides, photos of your notes, a text, or only a topic. For example: *"Lecture 5 of MATH 371 from this file, in Arabic"*.
3. Claude returns a complete file `lecture-05.mn`. Save it.
4. Website: the course → the lecture → **Student sheet → Upload .mn**.
5. Press **Preview** to check, then **Save**, then switch on **Show student sheet**.
:::

::: note "Figures in Python"
Claude draws the figures in Python. They are drawn **once, on your computer**, when you press **Save** or **Preview**. The first time the browser downloads Python (20–40 seconds); afterwards it is fast, and students receive the finished pictures instantly.
:::

::: proposition "Errors are local"
If the file has a mistake, a red box names it and its line. Copy the message to Claude in the same conversation: it returns the corrected complete file. Nothing reaches the students before **Save**.
:::

::: remark
You can also ask Claude for changes: *"add a figure for several values of $\alpha$"*, *"add three examples"*, *"make it Arabic"*, *"split it into two lectures"*. The **Sheet guide** shows a complete example that uses every element.
:::

## What a Student Sees

::: theorem "Solutions never leak" {#thm:leak}
(a) The solved sheet $D(F)$ can **never** be downloaded.
(b) The button **Download PDF** exists only on the student sheet and produces $T(F)$: a real A4 PDF (selectable text, same design) without solutions.
(c) Every sheet on screen and every downloaded PDF carries the student's **university ID** as a watermark.
:::

::: remarks
(1) The sheet behaves like a PDF viewer: zoom $-\ /\ +$, fit width ↔, **full screen** ⛶ (like F11), and contents ☰.
(2) While the student scrolls down, the top bar of the website disappears, so the whole screen is the sheet.
(3) The browser's Back button leaves the lecture and returns to the course page.
(4) Multiple-choice answers are checked instantly on the screen; they are **not** stored and no results are sent.
:::

::: illustration "Seeing it yourself"
Press **Student view** in the admin bar: you see the student area with every course open to you. **Back to admin** returns you to the panel.
:::

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Check |
|:---|:---|
| A student cannot see a lecture | the four conditions of (@eq:access) |
| A change does not appear | refresh the page (at most one hour) |
| A student forgot his password | ask the technical administrator to reset it |
| A red error box in the editor | copy it to Claude in the same conversation |
| A video does not play | the video must be **Unlisted**, not Private, on YouTube |

::: summary
► One door: **ahmadelajou.com/login** (@thm:door).
► Public content: **Website content → Add / ✏️ / 🗑 → Save**.
► Access is decided per course: **Approve** in **Requests** (@thm:access).
► One `.mn` file gives two sheets (@def:twosheets); Claude writes it, you **Upload → Preview → Save**.
► Students can download only the blank sheet, stamped with their ID (@thm:leak).
:::

::: mcq
Q: A student is approved in MATH 371. Can he open the lectures of MATH 372?
- Yes, approval is global
- Only the published ones
- No, every course is approved separately *
- Only after he signs in again
> By the corollary of @thm:access, approval in one course gives no access to another.

Q: Which sheet can a student download as a PDF?
- The solved sheet
- The student sheet, without solutions *
- Both
- Neither
> @thm:leak (b).

Q: You saved a new sheet but students do not see it. What is most likely missing?
- The video
- **Show student sheet** or **Published to students** *
- The course code
- A Python figure
> Check the four conditions of (@eq:access).
:::
